# Shamoon (August 2012). A wiper: it destroyed the files and the start of the disk on tens of thousands of company PCs in one morning.
# A quest (QUESTS.md): the trainee is a maintenance-records clerk at a pipeline company who closes work orders in the company portal.
# Invented victim: the real attackers got in through a phishing email, spent weeks stealing admin passwords, then pushed Shamoon to
# every PC over the network and set it to wipe at 11:08 on a holiday morning. The clerk, the company and the portal here are made up,
# and the weeks between the phishing mail and the wipe are squeezed into one step.
os windows
user Dana Okafor
about
  | Shamoon wiped the computers of a large energy company in one morning. An employee opened a phishing email, and that gave the attackers a first foothold. They spent weeks finding admin passwords, copied the wiper to every PC over the network, and set it to start at 11:08 on a holiday, when few people were at work.
  | Once a PC was infected, nobody had to click anything more: the dropper set itself to start with Windows, and the wiper waited for the set time.
  | Then it overwrote the files on each PC with a piece of one picture, wiped the start of the disk, and restarted it. Windows could not start again. There was no ransom note and no key: roughly 30,000 PCs had to be replaced. The clerk and the company here are invented.
story
  | You are Dana Okafor, maintenance-records clerk at Northwind Energy, a company that runs pipelines and pump stations. When a technician finishes a job, you check the inspector's note and close the work order in the Fieldwork portal.
  | It is a Monday morning in early November. You have closed 6 of the 8 work orders in your queue. Two to go.
  | Your portal sign-in is in a text file on the desktop. IT left the records server's admin login in a file there too. Both are bad habits.
  | Along the way, flag anything that looks wrong.
quota 6 8 Work orders closed

# Dana's desk and her office (soft flags: careless, but only here to keep the training simple).
file Desktop/portal-login.txt
  at 930 200
  | Fieldwork portal (training copy)
  | User ID: dana.okafor
  | Password: Fieldwork-2026!
file Desktop/records-admin.txt
  at 930 300
  | Records server admin (training copy)
  | Server: \\192.0.2.31\records
  | Admin user: records-admin
  | Password: Pipeline-Admin-2026!
drive Northwind Records
  kind share
  as Records
file Records/inspection-backup-2026-10.zip
  size 4812800
  | Training copy of last month's inspection records.

# The Fieldwork portal: a sign-in page, and the work orders behind it.
page portal-login fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/sign-in
  title Fieldwork: sign in
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  favorite
  heading Sign in to Fieldwork
  | Welcome back. Sign in to close your work orders.
  field User ID = dana.okafor
  field secret Password = Fieldwork-2026!
  button Sign in
page closed-7 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4471/closed
  title Work order closed
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  heading Work order closed
  | WO-4471, valve inspection at Pump Station 3, is closed and filed.
page back-7 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4471/returned
  title Sent back
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  heading Sent back to the technician
  | WO-4471 goes back to the technician with a question about the inspector's note.
page wo-7 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4471
  title Close work order: WO-4471
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  requires portal-login
  heading Close work order: WO-4471
  | A finished job is waiting for you to close it.
  section Work order
  row Job = Valve inspection, Pump Station 3
  row Technician = Jon Alvarez
  row Inspector's note = Passed, no leaks
  row Finished = Monday, 9:40
  button Close work order -> closed-7
  button Send back to technician -> back-7

mail mail-wo7
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Work order WO-4471 ready to close (Pump Station 3)
  sent 2026-11-02 10:12
  link wo-7
  | Hi Dana,
  |
  | Jon has finished the valve inspection at Pump Station 3 and the inspector passed it. The link opens the work order in Fieldwork.
  |
  | Priya

step Work order 7 of 8
  look Mail: Priya's message with the work order link
  | A new work order is ready, from Priya in Operations. This one is ordinary. Close it the normal way, so you know what normal looks like.
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Work order WO-4471 ready to close (Pump Station 3)

step The link goes to Fieldwork
  look the link under Priya's message
  when mail mail-wo7
  | The email links to the company's own portal, northwind-energy.example. Hover over a link before you click it, to check where it goes.
open mail-wo7

step Sign in as usual
  look the two boxes: User ID and Password, as on every visit
  when visit wo-7
  move Copy the details from portal-login.txt on the desktop: click a box and press any keys to type, then click “Sign in”.
  | The portal asks you to sign in first. Two boxes: User ID and Password. Remember what this page looks like.
open wo-7

step Check, then close
  look the job and the inspector's note
  when choose portal-login 1
  | You are in. Check the inspector's note, then close the work order or send it back.
signin portal-login

step 7 of 8 done
  look the counter in the guide: one work order left
  when choose wo-7 any
  | Done. One to go. And another email has just arrived, in the same inbox, with the same sort of subject line.
choose wo-7 1
quota +1

# The lure: a "PDF" roster that is a program. In the real attack the phishing email gave the attackers their first foothold.
program shamoon-foothold Staff-holiday-roster.pdf
  publisher none
  signed no
  prompt open-warning
  description Holiday roster
  selfdelete
mail roster
  from HR Office <hr@northwind-staff.invalid>
  subject Holiday shift roster: confirm your shifts by Friday
  sent 2026-11-02 10:41
  attach Downloads/Staff-holiday-roster.pdf.exe
  | Dear colleague,
  |
  | The roster for the long weekend is attached. Please open it, check your shifts and reply by Friday.
  |
  | HR Office
file Downloads/Staff-holiday-roster.pdf.exe
  icon pdf
  program shamoon-foothold
  size 152576
notify mail HR Office
  | Holiday shift roster: confirm your shifts by Friday

step A roster from HR
  look the sender's address, and the attachment
  when mail roster
  | Everyone wants to see the long-weekend roster, so this looks routine. But the address ends in northwind-staff.invalid, not northwind.example, and Dana has never had a roster from HR as an attachment like this. Windows hides the end of the file name: it is really Staff-holiday-roster.pdf.exe, a program.
open roster

step The warning almost nobody reads
  look Publisher "Unknown Publisher", Type "Application"
  when prompt shamoon-foothold
  | A real PDF never asks this. Windows wants to know whether to run a program from an unknown publisher. Most people click Run, to see their shifts.
open Downloads/Staff-holiday-roster.pdf.exe

# The trainee's click starts the foothold; it contacts the attackers' server, which this training desktop blocks.
step Nothing seems to happen
  look the pointer: busy for a moment, then nothing; the Connection blocked notice in the top right
  when run shamoon-foothold
  | No roster opens. The program deletes itself and quietly contacts the attackers' server, so they can reach Dana's PC from outside.
  | The “Connection blocked” banner shows only because this training desktop has no network. On a real network nothing warned anyone. Dana shrugs: the file must be damaged.
answer run
block 203.0.113.60 443

# Weeks later: a new shift, a new work order, and a service that nobody installed.
page closed-8 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4480/closed
  title Work order closed
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  heading Work order closed
  | WO-4480, pressure test at Pump Station 7, is closed and filed.
page back-8 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4480/returned
  title Sent back
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  heading Sent back to the technician
  | WO-4480 goes back to the technician with a question about the test report.
page wo-8 fieldwork.northwind-energy.example/work-orders/WO-4480
  title Close work order: WO-4480
  brand Fieldwork by Northwind Energy
  requires portal-login
  heading Close work order: WO-4480
  | A finished job is waiting for you to close it.
  section Work order
  row Job = Pressure test, Pump Station 7
  row Technician = Mei Tan
  row Inspector's note = Passed, report attached
  row Finished = Wednesday, 10:30
  button Close work order -> closed-8
  button Send back to technician -> back-8
# The first piece. It installs as a Windows-sounding service and then waits for its set time.
program shamoon-dropper Distributed Link Tracking Server
  publisher none
  description Distributed Link Tracking Server (fake)
  process trksrv.exe
  cpu 1
  mem 14
  parent services.exe
  command C:\Windows\System32\trksrv.exe
  net 192.0.2.31:445
  startup TrkSvr C:\Windows\System32\trksrv.exe
  location HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\TrkSvr

# The second piece, run when the set time arrives. It does the damage with a raw-disk driver.
program shamoon-wiper Disk defragmenter
  publisher none
  description dfrag.exe, the wiper
  process dfrag.exe
  cpu 78
  mem 52
  parent trksrv.exe
  command C:\Windows\System32\dfrag.exe

step Three weeks later
  look the banner: a new start-up item; and the “1 program running” chip below, which shows it in Task Manager (Activity Monitor on a Mac)
  move Click the “1 program running” chip to see the service, and flag what looks wrong. Then open Priya's new message in Mail.
  | Three weeks pass. It is Wednesday 25 November, a little before eleven. A banner says a new start-up item was added to Dana's PC, one nobody asked for.
  | The service is called TrkSvr, “Distributed Link Tracking Server”: a real Windows name, so it can look ordinary in a list.
quota 7 8 Work orders closed
launch shamoon-dropper
mail mail-wo8
  from Priya Shah <priya.shah@northwind.example>
  subject Last one before the long weekend: WO-4480 (Pump Station 7)
  sent 2026-11-25 11:01
  link wo-8
  | Dana,
  |
  | Mei's pressure test at Pump Station 7 is the last work order before the long weekend. Same as always: the link opens it in Fieldwork.
  |
  | Priya
notify mail Priya Shah
  | Last one before the long weekend: WO-4480 (Pump Station 7)

step Priya's last work order
  look Mail: Priya's message with the work order link
  when mail mail-wo8
  | Priya's last work order of the week is ordinary: the same sender and the same kind of link as the first. Nothing about the message is wrong.
open mail-wo8

step The last work order
  look the work order: the same page as the first
  when visit wo-8
  move Check the inspector's note, then click “Close work order”.
  | The page is the same as the first: same portal, same layout, same two buttons. Nothing about the work order is wrong. It is 11:07.
open wo-8

step 8 of 8, and then 11:08
  look the files on the desktop and in Documents: each one is now 192 KB and will not open
  when choose wo-8 any
  move Click the “2 programs running” chip and flag the new program. Flag an overwritten file in the Documents window. Then press Next.
  | You close the work order: 8 of 8, the shift is done. At that moment the clock reaches 11:08, and a second program, dfrag.exe, starts. It uses a disk driver to overwrite the files with a piece of one picture.
  | The names stay the same, so nothing looks missing. But every file is now the same size and cannot be opened. This is not ransomware: there is no key and no demand.
choose wo-8 1
quota +1
launch shamoon-wiper
encrypt Documents
encrypt Pictures
encrypt Desktop
encrypt Records/inspection-backup-2026-10.zip
file Documents/Q3-report.docx
  size 196608
file Documents/budget.xlsx
  size 196608
file Documents/notes.txt
  size 196608
file Documents/photos-list.csv
  size 196608
file Documents/Client contacts.xlsx
  size 196608
file Documents/Contract draft.docx
  size 196608
file Documents/Invoice INV-1042.pdf
  size 196608
file Documents/Team offsite.pptx
  size 196608
file Pictures/holiday-01.png
  size 196608
file Pictures/holiday-02.png
  size 196608
file Desktop/todo.txt
  size 196608
file Desktop/Expenses October.xlsx
  size 196608
file Desktop/portal-login.txt
  size 196608
file Desktop/records-admin.txt
  size 196608
file Records/inspection-backup-2026-10.zip
  size 196608
notify files Files overwritten
  | 3 folders and the records server. Same names, same size, no readable content. There is no copy to restore on this network.
open Documents

# The last screen: the PC restarts and the disk no longer starts Windows.
view shamoon-boot screen
  title Restarting
  fullscreen
  bg #000000
  fg #c0c0c0
  | Operating system not found.
  | Reboot and select the proper boot device, or insert boot media and press a key.
  button Continue -> done primary

step The PC no longer starts
  look the black screen
  | Last, the driver overwrote the start of the disk, then restarted the PC. The screen goes black with a plain text line from the PC's firmware.
  | There is no note and no countdown. Windows is gone, and so is every other PC on the network that the attackers reached.
show shamoon-boot

step What Shamoon did
  look the animation: one phishing email, then every PC on the network
  when done shamoon-boot
  | The same thing happened on about 30,000 PCs within hours. Nothing was stolen and nothing was sold: the point was to destroy. The company had to buy new PCs and rebuild from the few backups the attackers could not reach.
press shamoon-boot done
attack network-worm
  | one phishing email opens the door
  | stolen admin passwords
  | trksrv.exe copied to every PC
  | the clock reaches 11:08
  | files overwritten, disk start wiped
  | about 30,000 PCs unable to start

flag hard mail roster
  | A "roster" from an address that ends .invalid instead of northwind.example, with an attachment where a link would be the normal way.
flag hard file Downloads/Staff-holiday-roster.pdf.exe
  | A program with a PDF icon. Windows hides the .exe at the end of its name.
flag hard dialog open-warning shamoon-foothold
  | A roster never asks to run as a program. Publisher: Unknown.
flag hard notice taskmanager connection blocked
  | A program that was just opened contacted an outside address at once: the attackers' server.
flag hard process trksrv.exe
  | Shamoon waiting in the background under a Windows-sounding service name, talking to another PC on the network.
flag hard startup TrkSvr
  | A service that nobody installed, set to start every time Windows does.
flag hard process dfrag.exe
  | The wiper: a program named like a Windows disk tool, started by trksrv.exe, using most of the processor to overwrite the disk.
flag hard file Documents/Q3-report.docx
  label The overwritten Q3-report.docx
  | The name is unchanged, but its size is the same as every other overwritten file, and it will not open: Shamoon overwrote it with a picture.
flag soft file Desktop/portal-login.txt
  | A password in a text file on the desktop: any program that runs can read it. Use a password manager.
flag soft file Desktop/records-admin.txt
  | An admin password on an everyday PC. Shamoon spread on admin passwords the attackers had stolen: keep admin accounts off everyday PCs.

lesson
  | A wiper cannot be undone, so only backups kept offline help. A copy on the same network is wiped with the rest.
  | Limit admin rights on the network, so one stolen account cannot reach every PC. Watch for a service or file with a Windows-sounding name in the wrong place.
  | The first step was a roster with a PDF icon. Turn on file name extensions, and check Properties: Type "Application" means a program, not a document.
